    <h2>4. UTC-5 Offset Explained</h2>
    <p>
      The offset for Eastern Standard Time is written as **UTC-5** (or GMT-5). This notation indicates that EST is exactly five hours behind the global atomic baseline time. If it is 12:00 PM (noon) UTC, the time in the EST zone is 7:00 AM.
    </p>

