    </p>
    <p>
      An additional six states are split between the Eastern and Central time zones: Alabama (select regions), Florida (the western panhandle observes Central Time), Indiana (most of the state is on Eastern, but some western counties observe Central), Kentucky (split down the middle), Michigan (most observes Eastern, but counties bordering Wisconsin observe Central), and Tennessee (East Tennessee observes Eastern Time).
    </p>

