  <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
       SECTION 6: EST VS EDT
       ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section id="est-vs-edt" class="content-section reveal" aria-label="EST vs EDT">
    <h2>6. EST vs EDT: Seasonal Differences</h2>
    <p>
      The difference between EST and EDT is daylight saving time. Standard Time (EST) is observed during the winter, while Daylight Time (EDT) is observed during the summer.
    </p>
    <p>
      The seasonal shift is regulated to maximize afternoon sunlight during the spring, summer, and early autumn. In the U.S. and Canada, clocks transition from EST to EDT at 2:00 AM on the second Sunday of March, moving forward to 3:00 AM. They return to standard time at 2:00 AM on the first Sunday of November, moving back to 1:00 AM.
    </p>

    <!-- Custom Inline SVG: EST vs EDT Comparison Infographic (Infographic 3) -->
    <div style="margin: 2.5rem 0; text-align: center; border: 1px solid var(--line); padding: 1.5rem; border-radius: 12px; background: var(--panel);">
